#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""aquarium-app-helper: root side of FG-33 local apps (runtime units, builds,
ports, front-door includes, per-app secrets).

Installed root:root 0755 at /usr/local/sbin/aquarium-app-helper by
``aq_install_app_runtime`` (deploy/install/lib.sh). User ``hermes`` (the API
and ``hermes_cli/app_runtime.py``, never ``hermes-tools``) may run exactly
these verbs through sudo (deploy/sudoers.d/aquarium-apps), with NO further
arguments; the request is one JSON object on stdin:

    allocate    {"slug", "mode"}                       port + env file
    build       {"slug", "mode", "sha"[, "approval_ref"]}   build + point <mode> at it
    start       {"slug", "mode"}
    stop        {"slug", "mode"}
    restart     {"slug", "mode"}
    route       {"slug", "mode"}                       Caddy include (forward_auth)
    unroute     {"slug", "mode"}
    set-secret  {"slug", "mode", "name", "value"} | {..., "name", "delete": true}
    logs        {"slug", "mode"[, "lines", "build"]}
    status      {"slug", "mode"} | {"all": true}
    remove      {"slug", "mode", "confirm": "<slug>"}  irreversible: needs confirm
    configure   {} (read) | {["storage_base": "/abs/path"], ["min_free_mb": N],
                ["limits": {"member"|"admin": {"per_app": {..}, "per_member": {..}} | null}]}
                (Settings -> App storage / App limits; storage_base also sets
                APPS_BASE in /etc/aquarium/aquarium.conf for `aquarium apps db`)

The caller is UNTRUSTED: every field is validated here, ports come from the
box, never the request, and prod activation needs an ``approval_ref``.
Root-only argv forms (no sudo rule): ``status --all`` (deploy report) and
``idle-check <slug>-dev`` (the dev idle timer). ``run-app`` and ``build-run``
run unprivileged inside aquarium-app@ / aquarium-app-build@ units.

Layout (storage base from /etc/aquarium/apps.conf, default /var/lib/aquarium-apps):
    <base>/<slug>/releases/<mode>-<sha>/   root-owned built artifact (basePath is per mode)
    <base>/<slug>/<mode> -> releases/<mode>-<sha>
    /etc/aquarium/apps/<slug>/<mode>.env   PORT, HOSTNAME, APP_SLUG, APP_MODE, APP_BASE_PATH
    /etc/aquarium/apps/<slug>/<mode>/NAME  root 0600 credentials, one per file (APP_MCP_TOKEN, user secrets)
    /etc/aquarium/apps/<slug>/db-<mode>-{rw,ro}.dsn  written by `aquarium apps db create`;
                                           delivered as DATABASE_URL / DATABASE_URL_RO
    /etc/aquarium/apps/<slug>/ticket-<mode>.key      APP_TICKET_KEY (X-Aquarium-Principal key)
URL paths on the main site: prod /apps/<slug>, dev /apps-dev/<slug>.

Output is one JSON object on stdout. Exit 0 = done, 2 = rejected input,
3 = refused (capacity, busy build slot, missing confirmation),
1 = internal failure. Python 3 stdlib only.
"""

